From 49da4724710d3f231c2dc7a7729670ecc451dd82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tesseract XRT port <jwkim@limagin.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:09:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 01/19] xocl: include <linux/vmalloc.h> explicitly (Linux 6.10)

xocl_drv.h calls vzalloc() and the xocl sources use vmalloc(), vfree(),
vmap(), vunmap() and VM_MAP, but nothing includes <linux/vmalloc.h>.
Up to Linux 6.9 the header arrived through <linux/io.h> ->
<asm/io.h> -> <asm-generic/io.h>. Mainline commit 690da22dbfa8
("asm-generic/io.h: kill vmalloc.h dependency", v6.10) dropped that
include, so on 6.10+ every xocl object fails with implicit declarations.

Guard: none on purpose. <linux/vmalloc.h> exists on every kernel this
tree supports and is include-guarded; on <= 6.9 it is already part of
every translation unit, so the extra include changes nothing there.

Equivalence: header-only, no code change.

Upstream: same hunk as XRT commit 04350f685 ("Rebase #8555 - Build xrt
drivers on Linux 6.12-rc3"), path rewritten for the DKMS layout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SpY5QiU1d7kAe8YJM35EvA
---
 driver/xocl/xocl_drv.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/driver/xocl/xocl_drv.h b/driver/xocl/xocl_drv.h
index fc60699..e98f710 100644
--- a/driver/xocl/xocl_drv.h
+++ b/driver/xocl/xocl_drv.h
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@
 #include <linux/types.h>
 #include <linux/moduleparam.h>
 #include <linux/cdev.h>
+#include <linux/vmalloc.h>
 
 #include "xocl_types.h"
 #include "xclbin.h"
